From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Sepez <tsepez@google.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:45:50 -0700
Subject: Improve error handling in libjpeg encoding

Avoid ignoring fatal errors during Windows JPEG compression by using
longjmp to catch failures in libjpeg C wrapper functions, matching the
decompression architecture.

-- use modern memory ownership model.
-- avoid array of [1].

TAG=agy
CONV=2e125a78-6471-43e2-9eed-d2106f60cbec

Bug: 556853443
Change-Id: I2e5eadc41d277f2098ebc91be91d67578c10301f
Reviewed-on: https://pdfium-review.googlesource.com/c/pdfium/+/157030
Reviewed-by: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Tom Sepez <tsepez@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- jpegmodule.cpp include hunks: this branch predates the upstream
  include reshuffle (no IS_WIN-only include block, no
  libjpeg_scanline_decoder.h split), so only the functional part is
  taken: add fx_memory.h / fx_memory_wrappers.h (FxFreeDeleter) and
  drop the now-unused <type_traits>.
- The ScopedJpegCompressCommon helper is inserted after the branch's
  existing anonymous namespace in fxcodec (upstream had no code
  between `namespace fxcodec {` and JpegModule::CreateDecoder).
  jpeg_common.c/.h and the JpegEncode() body applied as upstream.

